export abstract anchor FactoryHarnesses:
    supportedHarnesses:
        The initial supported agent harnesses are Claude Code, Codex, and
        OpenCode. Each integration must accommodate API-backed and subscription
        accounts. The mapping of accounts and models to harnesses remains
        project configuration.
    commonAdapterContract:
        A common harness adapter contract isolates factory code from
        harness-specific behavior. Every integration provides the same
        operations behind it, while agents write and repair the
        environment-specific wiring that connects each harness. Factory code
        depends on the contract, not on one harness. Each adapter declares
        token, launch-request lookup, reference-only, or unsupported discovery.
    capabilityMinimums:
        A supported adapter must launch with a factory-generated attempt and
        launch request identifier that the harness retains or echoes, return a
        durable session reference, reconnect or report status for a known
        session, provide positive terminal evidence, cancel a session, and
        report usage when the harness exposes it. Capabilities are declared per
        harness and per account kind. An adapter that cannot launch, reconnect,
        report terminal evidence, or cancel is not supported for restart-
        recoverable work.
    evidenceMatrix:
        Each adapter declares its terminal evidence kinds, the precedence among
        sources, per-source freshness windows, and the mapping from terminal
        evidence to attempt outcome. Conformance checks the declared matrix
        against observed signals. Usage absence is a budget-unknown mode that
        requires engineer acceptance, records conservative exposure, and cannot
        claim a hard cap.
    adapterIdentityAndLease:
        The harness retains or echoes the attempt and launch request
        identifier. A session lease is claimed by exactly one session identity
        at adoption, and a second launch under a claimed lease is refused.
        Each session has a separate worktree and a per-session stop handle.
    requiredGuarantees:
        - launch a session for an assignment
        - resume or reconnect to a surviving session
        - observe liveness without mistaking a client disconnect for the end
        - request and confirm cancellation
        - report usage and allowance when the harness exposes it
    preservedReferences:
        Integrations preserve the session references needed to reconnect after
        a factory restart, so recovery does not launch duplicates. A missing or
        stale reference stays uncertain unless the integration can establish
        that the session ended.
    unresolvedHarnessDetails:
        The contract above is required. Per-harness implementation details
        remain: which exact signals are available, how the attempt token is
        injected, and how usage and artifacts are read. An adapter that cannot
        support a guarantee declares that capability unsupported, and the
        factory must not claim it.
